# Tab-separated: name<TAB>file<TAB>from<TAB>to<TAB>suite<TAB>filter.  `\n` becomes a newline.
#
# The first four lines each take the resolution back out of one handler — the exact bug the sweep
# was written to find, once per route that had it.  The fifth asks the opposite question: a
# resolver that returns the session's id *unconditionally* passes every `me` test and quietly
# reads the caller's own data for an explicit id, so it is checked against a suite that reads
# somebody else's thread.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

